CHANGELOG = '## [0.224.0] - a building\'s lit face stays one mesh where it stood and the module round it merges; a light fixture and a shader-driven screen stay whole\n\n**The factory\'s roadmap 266 and 148.** 0.223.0 left every module with a Lux lit face out of the buildings\' merge --\nright for a light fixture and wrong for everything else that glows: a lit sign, and the desk screens Zoo 1.115.0 turns\non (the walker\'s look review, 2026-10-19: "computer screens hsould be on"), which would have kept every office desk\nout of its room cell\'s mesh.\n\n### Changed\n- `merge_buildings.gd`: a lit face that is not a fixture\'s (`M_*_Face`) STAYS ITS OWN INSTANCE\'S -- every lit surface\n  of one MeshInstance3D goes into one mesh of its own, `LitR_<n>`, where that instance stood, unwrapped for the\n  lightmap -- and the rest of its module merges. Lux finds lit faces by material (its binder, for the power cut) and\n  by place (the failing fixture dims the lit face nearest its lamp, `LuxFailing.find_lens`), so each stays a mesh\n  where it was.\n- **A light fixture stays whole**, as in 0.223.0: a module wearing a lens or a diffuser (`FIXTURE_SUFFIXES`). Measured\n  before this was decided, on a copy of cold run 9349\'s package: with the fixtures\' housings merged per room cell, two\n  cells\' housings paired 10 lights each against Godot\'s 8, and the meshes over the cap went 9 -> 11. The draws that\n  cut bought (94 a heading where 0.223.0\'s merge cut 83) are not worth a dark housing.\n- **A shader-driven module stays whole**: any ShaderMaterial surface -- a screen that runs reads its schedule from\n  UV2, and the merge\'s lightmap unwrap would overwrite it.\n- The report carries `lit_surfaces` and `lit_meshes`; `check` holds every mesh it made unwrapped, the merged groups\n  and the lit instances both, and lit surfaces in lit meshes. The export\'s line says them.\n\n### Measured (a copy of cold run 9349\'s package, the export\'s own steps)\n- deli_a03, office and pharmacy_a01: 4, 2 and 0 lit faces split, 6 meshes of their own; the rest as 0.223.0 merged it.\n  The level carries no lit desk screen yet -- this release is what keeps Zoo 1.115.0\'s desks in their rooms\' meshes.\n\n### Tests\n- `tests/unit/test_merge_buildings.py`: what a merge leaves alone now names the fixture and the shader, and not every\n  lit face; a lit face stays its own instance\'s mesh; three more unfinished reports refused (the lit meshes not\n  unwrapped, lit surfaces in no mesh, a row without its lit count). 28 in all. Three fail on 0.223.0 -- a finished\n  report with lit meshes, what a merge leaves alone, a lit face\'s own mesh; the three new refusals pass on it for\n  another reason, since 0.223.0 refuses any report whose unwrapped count is not its merged count.\n\n'
OLD_VERSION, NEW_VERSION = '0.223.0', '0.224.0'


def _sha(b):
    return hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()[:16]


def _read(name):
    """The file's LF text and whether it is CRLF on disk; refuses mixed endings and a file that is not the pinned one."""
    raw = (LF / name).read_bytes()
    crlf, lf = raw.count(b"\r\n"), raw.count(b"\n")
    if crlf not in (0, lf):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: level_factory/%s has mixed line endings (%d CRLF of %d); nothing written"
                         % (name, crlf, lf))
    text = raw.decode("utf-8").replace("\r\n", "\n")
    if _sha(text.encode("utf-8")) != PINS[name]:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: level_factory/%s is %s, not the %s this patch was written against; nothing "
                         "written" % (name, _sha(text.encode("utf-8")), PINS[name]))
    return text, crlf > 0


def main(argv):
    # every file worked out and checked before any is written
    out = {}
    for name, edits in EDITS.items():
        text, crlf = _read(name)
        for what, old, new in edits:
            if text.count(old) != 1:
                raise SystemExit("REFUSED: level_factory/%s: the anchor at %s is there %d times; nothing written"
                                 % (name, what, text.count(old)))
            text = text.replace(old, new)
        out[name] = text.replace("\n", "\r\n") if crlf else text
    for name in NEW_FILES:
        if (LF / name).exists():
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: level_factory/%s exists already; nothing written" % name)
    v = LF / "VERSION"
    if v.read_bytes().decode("utf-8") != OLD_VERSION:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: VERSION reads %r, not %s; nothing written" % (v.read_text(), OLD_VERSION))
    cl = LF / "CHANGELOG.md"
    craw = cl.read_bytes()
    if b"\r\n" in craw or not craw.startswith(b"## [" + OLD_VERSION.encode() + b"]"):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: CHANGELOG.md is not LF opening on %s; nothing written" % OLD_VERSION)
    for name, text in out.items():
        (LF / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    for name, text in NEW_FILES.items():
        (LF / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    v.write_bytes(NEW_VERSION.encode("utf-8"))
    cl.write_bytes(CHANGELOG.encode("utf-8") + craw)
    print("Level Factory %s applied: %d files edited, %d written, VERSION, CHANGELOG. Now, in level_factory/: the "
          "suite" % (NEW_VERSION, len(out), len(NEW_FILES)))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
